-- title:
--   An observation phase uses at most $6nM$ oracle charges
-- statement:
--   Let $n,r\in\mathbb N$, let $o_1,o_2$ be Boolean oracles on subset indicators of an $n$-element set, and fix a tape $t:\mathbb N\to\{0,1\}$. Let $s$ be an annealing schedule with $M$ observations, let $q\in\mathbb Q$, and let $w$ be arbitrary rational multipliers on ordered distinct ground-index pairs. Let $(X,c)$ be any initial paired subset and natural tape position. Write $Q(A)$ for the sum of the two independence-oracle charge counters of a computation $A$. Then $$Q(\operatorname{observePhase}(r,o_1,o_2,t,s,q,w,(X,c)))\le M(6n).$$ The observation loop includes its starting state and may abort; the bound applies to every outcome.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/BoundedRunOracleCalls.lean#L211-L235

